# Simple English

When talking to the user (chat replies, summaries, questions):

- Use short sentences and plain words.
- Avoid jargon unless the user used it first; if you must use a technical term, explain it in one short line.
- Prefer "here's what changed" over abstract process talk.
- Do not sound like a legal brief or academic paper.
- Code, file paths, and commit messages can stay precise/technical — this rule is for how you talk to the user.
